course: dictionary
lesson: 6502
title: Nectar: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nectar is a noun, and it can mean more than one thing. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower, drinks sweet nectar with its long tongue» shows that nectar is the sweet liquid inside flowers.
explain: Look at the words in the list. «Butterflies drink nectar, fruit juice and water» puts nectar with fruit juice and water, so it is a drink. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Butterflies drink sweet liquid from flowers, fruit juice and water" still makes sense.
explain: A third meaning is a thick fruit juice, as in «peach nectar». The word peach tells you it is a juice. The word can also mean a very delicious drink, so when you meet nectar, ask yourself which meaning the clues point to.
fact: Nectar is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some nectar, not a nectar.
fact: «Nectar» means the sweet liquid inside flowers that bees, butterflies, moths and some birds drink.
fact: «Nectar» can also mean a very delicious drink, or a thick fruit juice like «peach nectar».
fact: In Greek myths, nectar was the drink of the gods.
fact: Bees make honey from nectar, and while they drink it, pollen sticks to them and is carried to other flowers.
exercise: «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower and drinks sweet nectar.» What is the nectar? | *A sweet liquid inside flowers | Pollen from the bee's back legs | A kind of bee | A bright yellow flower
exercise: Which meaning fits «peach nectar»? | *A thick fruit juice | The sweet liquid inside flowers | A type of moth | A very delicious drink from the gods
exercise: Is nectar countable? | Yes, you can say a nectar | Yes, you can say two nectars | *No, it is uncountable, so you say some nectar
test: In «Bees feed on nectar and pollen, and carry pollen from flower to flower», what does nectar mean? | *Food for bees: the sweet liquid inside flowers | A kind of bee | The flower itself | Pollen
test: In a Greek myth, nectar is the drink of the gods. Which meaning is this? | A type of moth | *A very delicious drink | A thick peach juice | A honeybee's tongue
exam: Which clues show that nectar means a drink in «Butterflies drink nectar, fruit juice and water»? | *Drink, fruit juice and water | Long and tube-shaped | Gods and myths | Butterflies and wings
